WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:06.005 line:0%
MATT GAETZ: Dr. Kahl, do we have
DOD personnel in Ukraine now?

00:00:06.038 --> 00:00:06.872 line:0%
COLIN KAHL: We do.

00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:08.474 line:0%
We have a couple
dozen at the embassy.

00:00:08.507 --> 00:00:10.410 line:0%
MATT GAETZ: Other than the
embassy, any other personnel?

00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:11.878 line:0%
COLIN KAHL: Nope.
MATT GAETZ: How about CIA?

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:13.346 line:0%
Are they training
folks in Ukraine?

00:00:13.379 --> 00:00:14.814 line:0%
COLIN KAHL: I'm not
going to talk about that

00:00:14.847 --> 00:00:16.649 line:0%
in an unclassified setting.

00:00:16.682 --> 00:00:19.085 line:0%
Happy to talk about that further
in the classified briefing.

00:00:19.118 --> 00:00:20.486 line:0%
MATT GAETZ: Is
the Azov Battalion

00:00:20.519 --> 00:00:23.523 line:0%
getting access to US weapons?

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:25.291 line:0%
COLIN KAHL: Not
that I'm aware of.

00:00:25.324 --> 00:00:28.728 line:0%
But if you have information--

00:00:28.761 --> 00:00:30.229 line:0%
MATT GAETZ: I
[INAUDIBLE] consent

00:00:30.262 --> 00:00:31.597 line:0%
to enter into the
record the Global

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:35.701 line:0%
Times investigative report
that talks about training.

00:00:35.734 --> 00:00:39.605 line:0%
It's from the Atlantic Council's
Digital Forensics Research Lab

00:00:39.638 --> 00:00:41.274 line:0%
citing the Azov Battalion
was even getting

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:42.875 line:0%
stuff as far back as 2018.

00:00:42.908 --> 00:00:44.043 line:0%
- Without objection, so ordered.

00:00:44.076 --> 00:00:45.244 line:0%
MATT GAETZ: Any
reason to disagree

00:00:45.277 --> 00:00:46.913 line:0%
with that assessment, Dr. Kahl?
COLIN KAHL: Is this the--

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:47.780 line:0%
I'm sorry.

00:00:47.814 --> 00:00:48.781 line:0%
Is this the Global
Times from China?

00:00:48.814 --> 00:00:51.484 line:0%
MATT GAETZ: No, this is--

00:00:51.517 --> 00:00:52.285 line:0%
well--

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:53.453 line:0%
COLIN KAHL: That's
what you read.

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:54.454 line:0%
MATT GAETZ: Yeah, it might be.

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:55.788 line:0%
Yeah, would that be a reason--

00:00:55.821 --> 00:00:57.457 line:0%
MATT GAETZ: I, as
a general matter,

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.058 line:0%
I don't take Beijing's
propaganda at face value.

00:00:59.091 --> 00:01:00.159 line:0%
MATT GAETZ: Well, no, no.

00:01:00.192 --> 00:01:01.661 line:0%
But just tell me if the
allegation is true or false.

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:02.895 line:0%
I mean--

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:04.097 line:0%
COLIN KAHL: I don't have any
evidence one way or the other.

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:06.199 line:0%
As a general matter, I don't
take Beijing's propaganda

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:07.033 line:0%
at face value.

00:01:07.066 --> 00:01:07.834
MATT GAETZ: Fair enough.

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:10.133
I would agree with
that assessment.

